Fullscreen view keeps the output size when the client commits another size

Problem: a fullscreen view takes any size the client commits as a client-initiated
resize and then sends that size back in a configure. Wine (winewayland) at scale 1.5
gets the fractional scale only after the first fullscreen configure, commits a stale
1707x960 once, and Wayfire then locks the window at 1707x960 (Deadlock, Proton). The
window does not cover the output, so it also cannot be scanned out. GNOME keeps the
output size, so the same game is fullscreen there.
Fix: while the view is fullscreen, treat a commit of another size like a commit of the
same size: show the buffer, keep the geometry, send no configure.
Upstream: not reported.
Remove when: upstream main keeps the size of fullscreen views on client commits. Check:
start Deadlock (PROTON_ENABLE_WAYLAND=1) at scale 1.5; window-rules/list-views shows
2560x1440, not 1707x960.
Base: wayfire 669bbe36.

